The Cryptographic Atlas uses separate licenses for educational content and
website source code.

Educational Content

The book content is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0). See LICENSE-CONTENT.

This includes:

- book/docs/**
- book/data/concept-cards/**
- book/data/diagrams/**
- book/data/comparison-matrices/**
- book/data/references.yml
- book/data/source-freshness.yml
- generated content artifacts under book/static/diagrams/**,
  book/static/img/diagrams/**, book/static/data/**, and
  book/static/downloads/**
- generated content data under book/src/generated/**
- repository documentation such as README.md unless stated otherwise

Website Source Code

Website source code is licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE-CODE.

This includes:

- book/src/components/**
- book/src/pages/**
- book/src/css/**
- book/scripts/**
- book/schemas/**
- book/docusaurus.config.ts
- book/sidebars.ts
- package metadata, TypeScript configuration, and CI configuration files

License Boundaries

If a file states a different license explicitly, that file's license controls.
Generated files inherit the license of the source material they are generated
from unless stated otherwise. Third-party dependencies and assets remain under
their own licenses.
